{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/808426-how-do-you-think-the-beings-of-the-owod-reacted-to-x-event","id":808426,"title":"How do you think the beings of the OWoD reacted to X event.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T20:41:47-08:00","id":808426,"title":"How do you think the beings of the OWoD reacted to X event.","content":"things like World War 2, The Gulf War, JFK's assassination or 9/11 . How do you think the supernatural's reacted to such events.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:28:32-08:00","id":808593,"title":"","content":"Depends on the being, really. Just like humans there were some that didn't care and some that cared a lot, regardless of being a supernatural or not they still run the gamut of reactions. Things that threatened the Kine population such as WW1 and 2 were probably taken a little more seriously and with more action versus something like JFK's assassination. I'm sure there was a vamp that helped plan that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T15:37:48-08:00","id":811351,"title":"","content":"for vampires at least probably very opportunistically for a good chunk of them. take 9/11 for example, it is very plausible for many Camerillia elders to stoke the fear and Islamaphobia that occured after the fact to justify or even cover up their actions against Assamites or Assamite assets in America and the Middle East. Just like many Tzimiece and Nephandi used the Holocaust and the violence in Eastern Europe around the 1990's for their experiments or to fuel their magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:33:25-08:00","id":812066,"title":"","content":"Most will just shake their heads and say, &quot;Humans. Sheesh.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:46:19-08:00","id":816099,"title":"","content":"I suspect that vampires would dislike large scale wars like WWI and WWII. They may not care about one group of humans persecuting or killing another group unless it directly affects their interests, when you have massive bombings and entire cities turned into ruin and rubble - that is dangerous even for elders and it ruins long laid plans. Vampires are inherently conservative creatures and so large upheavals are going to to be disliked, especially by entrenched elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T08:07:16-08:00","id":843968,"title":"","content":"What about all the vampire movies that got it close? Blade, Underworld, Queen of the damned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11404-knihowchowcow","name":"KniHowChowCow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:23:54-08:00","id":844067,"title":"","content":"Ratkin. Oh, less population, Good work!!<br /> <br /> Faes: Too much suffering means less glamour.<br /> <br /> Wraith: More new friends to the party!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T19:00:49-08:00","id":844267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KniHowChowCow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/808426-how-do-you-think-the-beings-of-the-owod-reacted-to-x-event?p=843968#post843968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about all the vampire movies that got it close? Blade, Underworld, Queen of the damned?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a debatable value of &quot;close&quot;. Vampire: The Masquerade does a number of things differently than all other vampire media, with any given one only being accurate to VtM vampires <i>some</i> of the time. Only a fraction of the Kindred population is likely to be depicted by coincidence in any given piece of pop culture. Even then, most of it is based on legends already leaked to the public.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the next point: mortals think of this stuff as fiction. If anything, inundating them with movies and books reinforces the public's certainty that vampires aren't real. Sure, vampires would <i>prefer </i>that mortals knew absolutely nothing about vampires, but making them know a lot of crap is the next best thing. Half of the films and books and video games about vampires were likely approved for production and release by executives thoroughly in the pocket of one Kindred or another. It makes sure that the public stays incredulous, and that there's plenty of disinformation floating around to trip up any mortals who do discover the truth.<br /> <br /> It also lets Kindred seed <i>really bad ideas</i> into the heads of potential hunters. Remember that woman from one of the Blade films who listened to music while hunting vampires? So she could have her own &quot;soundtrack&quot;? I wouldn't be surprised if a Kindred threw that in, just to see if any humans were vacuous enough to try it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:51:57-08:00","id":844388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/808426-how-do-you-think-the-beings-of-the-owod-reacted-to-x-event?p=844267#post844267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also lets Kindred seed <i>really bad ideas</i> into the heads of potential hunters. Remember that woman from one of the Blade films who listened to music while hunting vampires? So she could have her own &amp;quot;soundtrack&amp;quot;? I wouldn't be surprised if a Kindred threw that in, just to see if any humans were vacuous enough to try it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually listening to music loud in headphones is a suggestion in Hunters Hunted 2 so that it is harder for you to be subjected to the commands of dominate. <br /> <br /> It does make sense for vampires to spread disinformation though. I guess if someone keeps digging theyll either become a hunter, die, or be embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11404-knihowchowcow","name":"KniHowChowCow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T17:05:17-08:00","id":844808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KniHowChowCow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/808426-how-do-you-think-the-beings-of-the-owod-reacted-to-x-event?p=844388#post844388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually listening to music loud in headphones is a suggestion in Hunters Hunted 2 so that it is harder for you to be subjected to the commands of dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I read that part in Hunters Hunted 2. And it was just as stupid in that book as it was in the Blade movies. The potential benefit - drowning out the voice of a vampire - is outweighed by not being able to hear a vampire or ghoul sneaking up on you. Avoiding eye contact with the vampire has far few downsides. Or having earplugs that muffle voice, without the problem of distracting music.<br /> <br /> Thing about hunting monsters is that there are a large number of &quot;clever&quot; tricks people circulate about how to take them down. But &quot;clever&quot; is the NOT the same as &quot;wise&quot;. A thousand hunters likely met their end for being too clever for their own good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T08:33:34-07:00","id":851158,"title":"","content":"I always took 9/11 as a wake-up call to the Technocracy reminding them that mortals can and do change the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3197-david-michael-felt","name":"David Michael Felt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:47:54-07:00","id":856913,"title":"","content":"While Vampires would hate large Wars, it would also present them with the best possible &quot;time to take my rival out&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as historical events?<br /> <br /> I would imagine that Supernaturals did not like the A-Bomb drop (with the Garou hating all the testing)<br /> You could say some may have been provoked by one of the WOD denizens<br /> <br /> An interesting one would be how they would feel about now? (ie is Trump some sort of Malkavian prank on the Ventrue)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/433-jasoncarrier","name":"JasonCarrier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:43:55-07:00","id":857295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JasonCarrier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/808426-how-do-you-think-the-beings-of-the-owod-reacted-to-x-event?p=856913#post856913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Vampires would hate large Wars, it would also present them with the best possible &quot;time to take my rival out&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as historical events?<br /> <br /> I would imagine that Supernaturals did not like the A-Bomb drop (with the Garou hating all the testing)<br /> You could say some may have been provoked by one of the WOD denizens</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people would be reticent to like anything that caused Thunderwyrms to wake up and start eating in large numbers. &quot;Sandworms - you hate 'em, right?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"